====Verb====
{{wikidata lexeme|L14}}
{{en-verb}}

# {{senseid|en|to convey meaning}} {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[convey]] or [[communicate]]; to make [[known]] or [[explicit]].
#: {{syn|en|outspeak|utter|Thesaurus:communicate}}
#: {{cot|en|put|t1=express (something) in a certain manner}}
#: {{ux|en|Words cannot '''express''' the love I feel for him.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=5|passage=We '''expressed''' our readiness, and in ten minutes were in the station wagon, rolling rapidly down the long drive, for it was then after nine. We passed on the way the van of the guests from Asquith. As we reached the lodge we heard the whistle, and we backed up against one side of the platform as the train pulled up at the other.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Christina Maxouris; Doug Criss|title=Everything you wanted to know about Yom Kippur|url=https://www.cnn.com/2019/10/08/us/yom-kippur-meaning-trnd/index.html|date=2019-10-08|passage=Services during Yom Kippur are held continuously through the day and include readings from the Torah and the reciting of prayers '''expressing''' regret or asking for forgiveness.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20200806081259/https://www.cnn.com/2019/10/08/us/yom-kippur-meaning-trnd/index.html}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Kate Bennett|title=Michelle Obama to 2020 graduates: ‘For those of you who feel invisible: Please know that your story matters’|url=https://www.cnn.com/2020/06/07/politics/michelle-obama-race-relations-2020-commencement|date=2020-06-07|passage=Obama '''expresses''' empathy for graduates who might be feeling lost or overwhelmed, adding she, too, feels those emotions.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221006044622/https://edition.cnn.com/2020/06/07/politics/michelle-obama-race-relations-2020-commencement}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[press]], [[squeeze]] out (especially said of [[milk]]).
#* {{RQ:Melville Moby-Dick|[[s:Moby-Dick (1851) US edition/Chapter 13|chapter 13]]|text=The people of his island of Rokovoko, it seems, at their wedding feasts '''express''' the fragrant water of young cocoanuts into a large stained calabash like a punchbowl {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1949|journal=United States Naval Medical Bulletin|volume=49|issue=1|page=61
|passage=It contained many cysts which were filled with sagolike granules that could be '''expressed''' under pressure.}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|date=15 March 2018|title=Platypus milk: unlikely weapon in fight against superbugs|author=Kelsey Munroe|url=https://www.theguardian.com/society/2018/mar/15/platypus-milk-unlikely-weapon-in-fight-against-superbugs
|passage=They don’t have teats, so the mothers '''express''' their milk onto their bellies for their young to feed.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20180427164559/https://www.theguardian.com/society/2018/mar/15/platypus-milk-unlikely-weapon-in-fight-against-superbugs}}
# {{lb|en|biochemistry}} To [[translate]] [[messenger RNA]] into [[protein]].
# {{lb|en|biochemistry}} To [[transcribe]] [[deoxyribonucleic acid]] into messenger RNA.
#* {{RQ:Wired|date=2015-11-28|author=Ferris Jabr|title=How Humans Ended Up With Freakishly Huge Brains|url=http://www.wired.com/2015/11/how-humans-ended-up-with-freakishly-huge-brains/
|passage=When a cell “'''expresses'''” a gene, it translates the DNA first into a signature messenger RNA (mRNA) sequence and subsequently into a chain of amino acids that forms a protein.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160306173630/https://www.wired.com/2015/11/how-humans-ended-up-with-freakishly-huge-brains/}}

